 `packages/orchestration/artifact_preview.py` and their three test files, remove the `artifacts`
 entry and `_build_artifacts_json` from `packages/orchestration/ui_server.py` and the two lines
 from `tests/orchestration/import_reachability_allowlist.txt`, and delete this paragraph.
+
+## DECISION F041 D2 — the file route serves exactly two kinds of name, `README.md` from either root as plain text and one image directly under the evidence root's `captures/`, each at most 10 MiB, with headers that keep a served file from ever running as a page; and the static asset route's containment becomes a path test (R-1105) (2026-09-29)
+
+CONTEXT: DECISION F041 D1 (5) left the file route to this round: the cockpit needs a screenshot's bytes for the grid and the lightbox, and a README over 256 KiB needs its whole text behind an "open full file" link. Measured by the reviewer at `e1dc49dd`: `do_GET` in `packages/orchestration/ui_server.py` dispatches single-segment job endpoints from its `handlers` dict and deeper ones as structural routes, which `_walkable_paths` of `tests/ui_server/test_command_channel.py` must list by hand; `_send_json` sets only `Content-Type`, `Content-Length` and `Cache-Control`; and `_serve_static` tests containment by a string prefix, which R-1105 records.
+
+CHOSEN: (1) THE ROUTE is `/api/jobs/<id>/artifacts/file?root=<root>&path=<name>`, structural, answered by `read_artifact_file` in `packages/orchestration/artifact_preview.py`. (2) TWO NAMES ARE SERVABLE: `README.md` from the workspace or the evidence root, as `text/plain; charset=utf-8`, and `captures/<one file>` from the evidence root whose suffix is in `IMAGE_CONTENT_TYPES`, as that type; the name must already be in normal form. Any other request answers 400 `invalid artifact request` before the disk is read; a name that does not resolve through `resolve_artifact_path` answers 404 `artifact not found`; a file over `FILE_MAX_BYTES`, 10 MiB, answers 413 `artifact too large`; every refusal is JSON. (3) THE HEADERS of every served file are `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; sandbox` and `Cache-Control: no-store`, so a file opened directly in a tab cannot run script, load anything or be sniffed into another type. (4) R-1105: `_serve_static` refuses a target that is not `is_relative_to` the resolved `dist`.
+
+ALTERNATIVES: serving any file under a root, rejected because the view lists exactly these two kinds and a wider route would serve evidence the cockpit never shows; serving the README as `text/markdown`, rejected because a browser may render an unknown type it sniffs and plain text is what "open full file" means; streaming files in chunks, rejected because the cap bounds every body at 10 MiB.
+
+HOW TO REVERSE: delete `read_artifact_file`, `ArtifactFile`, `FILE_MAX_BYTES` and `README_CONTENT_TYPE` from `artifact_preview.py`, the route, `_read_artifact_file` and `_send_artifact_bytes` from `ui_server.py`, their tests and the `_walkable_paths` line, and this paragraph; R-1105's repair stands on its own.
